{
  "slug": "theory-of-formal-languages",
  "title": "Theory of Formal Languages",
  "tags": [
    "field/cs",
    "subject/automata",
    "concept/2.1/theory"
  ],
  "htmlContent": "<p>In plain English, we distinguish 3 different entities:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Letters</li>\n<li>Words</li>\n<li>Sentences</li>\n</ol>\n<p>A group of letters make a words, a group of which makes sentences.</p>\n<p>However, not all collections of letters form valid words, and not all collections of words form valid sentences. Therefore we need a strong theoretical foundation from which our language is built.</p>\n<p>To construct a general <strong>theory of formal languages</strong>, we need to have the definition of a <strong>language structure</strong>, in which the decision of whether a given string of units constitutes a valid larger unit is not a matter of guesswork, but clear and explicit rules.</p>\n<p>In this model, we will consider language as symbols with <em>formal</em>\n(i.e. the form of the string as in what constitutes a valid string format, not the meaning. This is important as most of our sets might look like gibberish) rules.</p>\n<hr>\n<h2>Basic Definitions:</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>A finite, non-empty set of symbols (letters) is called an <strong>alphabet</strong>, denoted by the letter <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Σ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">Σ</span></span></span></span> (Sigma).\n<ul>\n<li>Essentially just a set of letters that we can use to construct strings and, when label them as words once they are part of a \"Language\".</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>A <strong>string</strong> is a concatenation of finite symbols from the alphabet.\n<ul>\n<li>e.g. if <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Σ</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mi>a</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\Sigma = \\{a,b\\}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">Σ</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">{</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">a</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">b</span><span class=\"mclose\">}</span></span></span></span> then a string would be any combination of these, such as <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>a</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>b</mi><mi>b</mi><mi>b</mi><mi>b</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">aaaaa, bbbb, abab</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8889em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">aaaaa</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">bbbb</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">abab</span></span></span></span></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>A <strong>word</strong> is a string that belongs to some language.\n<ul>\n<li>e.g. if <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Σ</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\Sigma = \\{x\\}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">Σ</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">{</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"mclose\">}</span></span></span></span> and a language L is defined as <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>:</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mn>3...</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">L = \\{x^n: n = 1,2,3 ...\\}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">L</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">{</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.6644em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">n</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">:</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">n</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">3...</span><span class=\"mclose\">}</span></span></span></span>, then <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>x</mi><mi>x</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>x</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">.</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">.</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">.</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x, xx, xxx ...</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.625em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">xx</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">xxx</span><span class=\"mord\">...</span></span></span></span> are all words</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h5>- Empty String (Null String):</h5>\n<ul>\n<li>A string can also have no letters, this is called the <strong>empty string</strong> or <strong>null string</strong>, denoted by the symbol Λ.</li>\n<li>If Λ is a word in a language, it represents a word with zero letters.</li>\n<li>Important note: Λ is <strong>not</strong> considered a symbol of any alphabet.\n<ul>\n<li>Example: If L = {x, xx, xxx …}, then Λ ∉ L unless explicitly added.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>The language with no words at all is denoted by ∅ (null set).\n<ul>\n<li>In ∅, even Λ is not present since there are no words at all.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h5>- Length:</h5>\n<ul>\n<li>The <strong>length</strong> of a string is the number of symbols in it.\n<ul>\n<li>Notation: <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∣</mi><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∣</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|w|</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">∣</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0269em;\">w</span><span class=\"mord\">∣</span></span></span></span> = length of string <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">w</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0269em;\">w</span></span></span></span>.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Examples:\n<ul>\n<li>If <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a = xxxx</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">a</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">xxxx</span></span></span></span>, then <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∣</mi><mi>a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∣</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|a| = 4</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">∣</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">a</span><span class=\"mord\">∣</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">4</span></span></span></span>.</li>\n<li>If <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>428</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">c = 428</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">c</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">428</span></span></span></span>, then <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∣</mi><mi>c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∣</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|c| = 3</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">∣</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">c</span><span class=\"mord\">∣</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">3</span></span></span></span>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∣</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Λ</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∣</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|\\Lambda| = 0</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">∣Λ∣</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0</span></span></span></span>.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>In general, if <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∣</mi><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∣</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|w| = 0</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">∣</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0269em;\">w</span><span class=\"mord\">∣</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0</span></span></span></span>, then <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Λ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">w = \\Lambda</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0269em;\">w</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">Λ</span></span></span></span>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h5>- Concatenation:</h5>\n<ul>\n<li>Concatenation means writing two strings side by side to form a longer string.</li>\n<li>If <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a = xxx</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">a</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">xxx</span></span></span></span> and <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">b = xx</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">b</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">xx</span></span></span></span>, then <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">ab = xxxxx</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">ab</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">xxxxx</span></span></span></span>.</li>\n<li>Generally, if <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a = x^n</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">a</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6644em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.6644em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">n</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> and <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">b = x^m</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">b</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6644em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.6644em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">m</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>, then <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">ab = x^{n+m}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">ab</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.7713em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.7713em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">n</span><span class=\"mbin mtight\">+</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">m</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>.\n<ul>\n<li>Example: If <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mi>x</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>x</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>x</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>x</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">.</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">.</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">.</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">L = \\{x, xxx, xxxxx ...\\}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">L</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">{</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">xxx</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">xxxxx</span><span class=\"mord\">...</span><span class=\"mclose\">}</span></span></span></span> then <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a=xxx</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">a</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">xxx</span></span></span></span> and <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">b=xxxxx</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">b</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">xxxxx</span></span></span></span> are words in L, but <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">ab=xxxxxxxx</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">ab</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">xxxxxxxx</span></span></span></span> is <strong>not</strong> in L.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Therefore, concatenation does not always produce a word in the same language.</li>\n</ul>\n<hr>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>NEXT:</strong> <a href=\"/notes/kleenes-and-positive-closure\">2.2 Kleene's and Positive Closure</a></p>",
  "rawMarkdown": "\nIn plain English, we distinguish 3 different entities:\n\n1) Letters\n2) Words\n3) Sentences\n\nA group of letters make a words, a group of which makes sentences.\n\nHowever, not all collections of letters form valid words, and not all collections of words form valid sentences. Therefore we need a strong theoretical foundation from which our language is built.\n\nTo construct a general **theory of formal languages**, we need to have the definition of a **language structure**, in which the decision of whether a given string of units constitutes a valid larger unit is not a matter of guesswork, but clear and explicit rules.\n\nIn this model, we will consider language as symbols with *formal*\n(i.e. the form of the string as in what constitutes a valid string format, not the meaning. This is important as most of our sets might look like gibberish) rules.\n- - -\n## Basic Definitions:\n- A finite, non-empty set of symbols (letters) is called an **alphabet**, denoted by the letter $\\Sigma$ (Sigma).\n\t- Essentially just a set of letters that we can use to construct strings and, when label them as words once they are part of a \"Language\". \n- A **string** is a concatenation of finite symbols from the alphabet.\n\t-  e.g. if $\\Sigma = \\{a,b\\}$ then a string would be any combination of these, such as $aaaaa, bbbb, abab$\n- A **word** is a string that belongs to some language. \n\t- e.g. if $\\Sigma = \\{x\\}$ and a language L is defined as $L = \\{x^n: n = 1,2,3 ...\\}$, then $x, xx, xxx ...$ are all words\n##### - Empty String (Null String):\n- A string can also have no letters, this is called the **empty string** or **null string**, denoted by the symbol Λ.\n- If Λ is a word in a language, it represents a word with zero letters.\n- Important note: Λ is **not** considered a symbol of any alphabet.\n\t- Example: If L = {x, xx, xxx …}, then Λ ∉ L unless explicitly added.\n- The language with no words at all is denoted by ∅ (null set).  \n    - In ∅, even Λ is not present since there are no words at all.\n##### - Length:\n- The **length** of a string is the number of symbols in it.  \n\t- Notation: $|w|$ = length of string $w$.\n- Examples:\n  - If $a = xxxx$, then $|a| = 4$.\n  - If $c = 428$, then $|c| = 3$.\n  - $|\\Lambda| = 0$.\n- In general, if $|w| = 0$, then $w = \\Lambda$.\n##### - Concatenation:\n- Concatenation means writing two strings side by side to form a longer string.\n- If $a = xxx$ and $b = xx$, then $ab = xxxxx$.\n- Generally, if $a = x^n$ and $b = x^m$, then $ab = x^{n+m}$.\n\t- Example: If $L = \\{x, xxx, xxxxx ...\\}$ then $a=xxx$ and $b=xxxxx$ are words in L, but $ab=xxxxxxxx$ is **not** in L.\n- Therefore, concatenation does not always produce a word in the same language.\n---\n---\n**NEXT:** [2.2 Kleene's and Positive Closure](/notes/kleenes-and-positive-closure)\n",
